  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/gorc1/). VERDICT: PARTLY-STALE. 2026-11-01 review (dev 100b6fbb6e): symptom holds - io-boundaries on the _INCOMING fixture shows net_recv TcpListener.incoming and no TcpStream.read_to_end. Stated cause does not: there is no TcpStream.unwrap row any more and stream.zork() on the loop var resolves rust:external:0-0:zork, so the loop variable is untyped rather than mistyped as TcpStream. let s = listener.accept().unwrap().0 is untyped too. Commit that removed the unwrap attribution not identified. MECHANISM: no element type inferred for a for-pattern over an iterator (nor tuple/field projection of accept())."  # 1ca5
